<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to July 5.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to July 5.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to July 5 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week June 29 - July 5</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97	  30,213 tns	  1,684 tns     5.57 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	  42,452 tns	  2,540 tns     5.98 pct</p>
<p>     94-95	  30,148 tns	  2,825 tns     9.37 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to July 5</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    42,132,051 tns    4,541,637 tns    10.78 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    40,160,117 tns    4,374,665 tns    10.89 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    40,109,276 tns    4,276,259 tns    10.66 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week, 3 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 2 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 2 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>Final sugar crop figures were expected later in the day.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
